{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc | sed -n '1,180p;600,714p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '1260,1465p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.head\n     2\t  \"The published head trace and its rule (docs/design/\n     3\t   yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md, slice H0): a publisher's index HEAD as a\n     4\t   signed trace, and the pure judgement a reader makes of one.\n     5\t\n     6\t   A trace is exactly the closed shape of 5.2:\n     7\t\n     8\t     {:yin.head/envelope {:yin.head/principal \\\"ed25519:<64 hex>\\\"\n     9\t                          :yin.head/manifest  :segment/...\n    10\t                          :yin.head/seq       n}\n    11\t      :yin.head/proof    {:yin.head/signature \\\"<128 hex>\\\"}}\n    12\t\n    13\t   signed over `yin.head/trace:v1\\\\n` and the envelope's canonical bytes\n    14\t   (`yin.vm.linker.sign/sign-trace`).  The sequence is derived, never\n    15\t   stored: the greatest transaction `t` among the datoms of the index the\n    16\t   manifest names (`seq-of`).\n    17\t\n    18\t   Return shapes this namespace chose where the design leaves them open:\n    19\t   - `judge` answers one keyword, the outcome of the 5.5 table:\n    20\t     `:yin.head/malformed`, `:yin.head/wrong-principal`,\n    21\t     `:yin.head/bad-proof`, `:yin.head/stale`, `:yin.head/equivocation`,\n    22\t     `:duplicate` or `:candidate`.  Its `principal` is the followed\n    23\t     principal id, `\\\"ed25519:\\\"` and 64 lowercase hex; `floor` is a\n    24\t     sequence or nil; `installed` is the installed head's manifest\n    25\t     address, or nil.\n    26\t   - A sequence is a nonnegative integer no greater than 2^53 - 1, the\n    27\t     greatest integer every host holds exactly (5.10: the sequence stays\n    28\t     within 2^53); beyond it a trace is `:yin.head/malformed`.\n    29\t   - `trace` throws `ex-info` when the key or the trace it would build is\n    30\t     not well formed; it never answers a malformed trace.\n    31\t\n    32\t   Slice H1 adds the board and the follower (5.1, 5.3 to 5.7, section 6),\n    33\t   over any `dao.stream` reader handle: the follower calls only `cursor`\n    34\t   and `next` on it.  Return shapes chosen where the design leaves them\n    35\t   open:\n    36\t   - `deposit!` answers `{:status :ok :trace t}` (a trace equal to the\n    37\t     board's current one is not appended again) or `{:status :refused\n    38\t     :reason r ...}`, `r` one of `:yin.head/seq-collision`,\n    39\t     `:yin.head/seq-regression`, `:yin.head/empty`, `:yin.head/no-key`.\n    40\t   - `follow` answers `[follower node]`: the node records the installed\n    41\t     head of each persisted record (`yin.vm.linker.dht/installed-heads`).\n    42\t     A record that fails, or more than 64 principals, throws `ex-info`\n    43\t     with `:yin.head/refused` naming the reason and the principal.\n    44\t   - `step` and `install` answer `[follower node events]`.  An event is\n    45\t     `{:yin.head/event e :principal p ...}`: `:confirmed` and\n    46\t     `:installed` with `:trace`; `:refused` with `:reason` and `:trace`\n    47\t     (`install` of a trace that is not the confirmed one is refused\n    48\t     `:yin.head/not-confirmed`, follower and node unchanged);\n    49\t     `:unloadable` with `:trace` and `:failure`; `:source-lost` with\n    50\t     `:outcome`.\n    51\t   - `moved` answers `[{:name n :linked a :resolved b} ...]` by name.\"\n    52\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    53\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    54\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    55\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    56\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    57\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    58\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    59\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(def ^:private max-seq\n    63\t  \"2^53 - 1: the greatest integer exact on every host.\"\n    64\t  9007199254740991)\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(def ^:private hex-digits \"0123456789abcdef\")\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(defn- hex?\n    71\t  [n s]\n    72\t  (and (string? s)\n    73\t       (= n (count s))\n    74\t       (every? #(some? (str/index-of hex-digits (str %))) s)))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn- valid-seq?\n    78\t  [n]\n    79\t  (and (integer? n) (<= 0 n max-seq)))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- public-of-principal\n    83\t  \"The 64 hex digits of an `ed25519:` principal id, or nil.\"\n    84\t  [principal]\n    85\t  (when (and (string? principal) (str/starts-with? principal \"ed25519:\"))\n    86\t    (let [public (subs principal (count \"ed25519:\"))]\n    87\t      (when (hex? 64 public) public))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- well-formed?\n    91\t  \"The closed shape of 5.2, with a sequence that is a nonnegative\n    92\t   integer.\"\n    93\t  [trace]\n    94\t  ;; Each value is checked `map?` with its closed key set before anything\n    95\t  ;; is read from it: a trace comes off a channel and may decode to any\n    96\t  ;; shape.\n    97\t  (try\n    98\t    (boolean\n    99\t      (and (map? trace)\n   100\t           (= #{:yin.head/envelope :yin.head/proof} (set (keys trace)))\n   101\t           (let [envelope (get trace :yin.head/envelope)\n   102\t                 proof (get trace :yin.head/proof)]\n   103\t             (and (map? envelope)\n   104\t                  (= #{:yin.head/principal :yin.head/manifest :yin.head/seq}\n   105\t                     (set (keys envelope)))\n   106\t                  (map? proof)\n   107\t                  (= #{:yin.head/signature} (set (keys proof)))\n   108\t                  (public-of-principal (get envelope :yin.head/principal))\n   109\t                  (jing/segment-address? (get envelope :yin.head/manifest))\n   110\t                  (valid-seq? (get envelope :yin.head/seq))\n   111\t                  (hex? 128 (get proof :yin.head/signature))))))\n   112\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn trace\n   116\t  \"Build and sign the trace of `manifest` at sequence `n` under `key`,\n   117\t   `{:seed hex :public hex}`.  The principal is the key's own.\"\n   118\t  [key manifest n]\n   119\t  (let [principal (sign/principal (sign/public-of (:seed key)))\n   120\t        envelope {:yin.head/principal principal\n   121\t                  :yin.head/manifest manifest\n   122\t                  :yin.head/seq n}\n   123\t        built {:yin.head/envelope envelope\n   124\t               :yin.head/proof (sign/sign-trace (:seed key) envelope)}]\n   125\t    (when-not (well-formed? built)\n   126\t      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed head trace\"\n   127\t                      {:reason :yin.head/malformed :envelope envelope})))\n   128\t    built))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- proven?\n   132\t  [trace]\n   133\t  (sign/verify-trace (public-of-principal\n   134\t                       (get-in trace [:yin.head/envelope :yin.head/principal]))\n   135\t                     (jing/canonical-bytes (:yin.head/envelope trace))\n   136\t                     (get-in trace [:yin.head/proof :yin.head/signature])))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn verify\n   140\t  \"True when `trace` has the closed shape of 5.2 and its signature is its\n   141\t   principal's head proof over its envelope; false otherwise.  Never\n   142\t   throws.\"\n   143\t  [trace]\n   144\t  (try\n   145\t    (boolean (and (well-formed? trace) (proven? trace)))\n   146\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn seq-of\n   150\t  \"The greatest transaction `t` among `datoms`; nil for no datoms.\"\n   151\t  [datoms]\n   152\t  (when (seq datoms)\n   153\t    (reduce max (map index/datom-t datoms))))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn judge\n   157\t  \"The rule of 5.5 for one observed trace: a pure function of the\n   158\t   followed `principal`, the `floor` (the installed head's sequence, or\n   159\t   nil), the `installed` manifest and the `trace`.  It takes no source\n   160\t   and no candidate: its answer is the same whoever carried the trace,\n   161\t   in whatever order, and whatever is loading.\"\n   162\t  [principal floor installed trace]\n   163\t  ;; The shape is checked before any field is read: `judge` never throws,\n   164\t  ;; whatever a channel decoded the trace to.\n   165\t  (if-not (well-formed? trace)\n   166\t    :yin.head/malformed\n   167\t    (let [{:yin.head/keys [manifest] n :yin.head/seq}\n   168\t          (:yin.head/envelope trace)]\n   169\t      (cond\n   170\t        (not= principal (:yin.head/principal (:yin.head/envelope trace)))\n   171\t        :yin.head/wrong-principal\n   172\t        (not (verify trace)) :yin.head/bad-proof\n   173\t        (nil? floor) :candidate\n   174\t        (< n floor) :yin.head/stale\n   175\t        (and (= n floor) (= manifest installed)) :duplicate\n   176\t        (= n floor) :yin.head/equivocation\n   177\t        :else :candidate))))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t;; =============================================================================\n   600\t   [{:yin.head/event :unloadable :principal principal :trace (:trace cand)\n   601\t     :failure failure}]])\n   602\t\n   603\t\n   604\t(defn- settle\n   605\t  \"Advance `principal`'s candidate against its record: `[follower node\n   606\t   events]`.\"\n   607\t  [follower node principal now]\n   608\t  (let [{:keys [candidate]} (get-in follower [:principals principal])\n   609\t        m (:manifest candidate)\n   610\t        status (when candidate (dht/load-status node m))]\n   611\t    (cond\n   612\t      (or (nil? candidate) (= :confirmed (:state candidate)))\n   613\t      [follower node []]\n   614\t\n   615\t      ;; the record was removed under the follower: start it again\n   616\t      (nil? status)\n   617\t      (let [[follower node] (acquire follower node principal m)]\n   618\t        [(assoc-in follower [:principals principal :candidate :state] :loading)\n   619\t         node []])\n   620\t\n   621\t      (= :loading (:status status))\n   622\t      [(assoc-in follower [:principals principal :candidate :state] :loading)\n   623\t       node []]\n   624\t\n   625\t      (= :loaded (:status status))\n   626\t      (let [{:keys [datoms failure]} (loaded-datoms-of node m status)\n   627\t            n (:seq candidate)]\n   628\t        (cond\n   629\t          failure\n   630\t          (if (= :failed (:state candidate))\n   631\t            [follower node []]\n   632\t            (let [[follower events] (unloadable follower principal candidate\n   633\t                                                now failure)]\n   634\t              [follower node events]))\n   635\t\n   636\t          (= n (seq-of datoms))\n   637\t          [(assoc-in follower [:principals principal :candidate :state]\n   638\t                     :confirmed)\n   639\t           node\n   640\t           [{:yin.head/event :confirmed :principal principal\n   641\t             :trace (:trace candidate)}]]\n   642\t\n   643\t          :else\n   644\t          (let [[follower node] (release follower node principal m)\n   645\t                trace (:trace candidate)]\n   646\t            [(update-in follower [:principals principal] assoc\n   647\t                        :candidate nil\n   648\t                        :rejected (envelope-id trace)\n   649\t                        :refusal {:reason :yin.head/seq-mismatch :trace trace\n   650\t                                  :index-seq (seq-of datoms)})\n   651\t             node\n   652\t             [(assoc (refused-event principal :yin.head/seq-mismatch trace)\n   653\t                     :index-seq (seq-of datoms))]])))\n   654\t\n   655\t      ;; the load failed: report it once, then start it again after the\n   656\t      ;; delay, under the kind the record had\n   657\t      (not= :failed (:state candidate))\n   658\t      (let [[follower events] (unloadable follower principal candidate now\n   659\t                                          (:reason status))]\n   660\t        [follower node events])\n   661\t\n   662\t      (< now (:due candidate)) [follower node []]\n   663\t\n   664\t      :else\n   665\t      (if-some [walk (walk-of (:kind status) m)]\n   666\t        [(update-in follower [:principals principal :candidate] assoc\n   667\t                    :state :loading\n   668\t                    :due nil\n   669\t                    :delay (min (* 2 (:delay candidate))\n   670\t                                (:repair-max-ticks follower)))\n   671\t         (-> (dht/forget node m)\n   672\t             (dht/load m {:kind (:kind status) :walk walk}))\n   673\t         []]\n   674\t        [follower node []]))))\n   675\t\n   676\t\n   677\t(defn step\n   678\t  \"One pass after `dao.space.dht/step` at the owner's reading `now`: poll\n   679\t   each followed source that is due, judge what it shows, keep one\n   680\t   candidate per principal, and advance each candidate's load.  It\n   681\t   confirms; it never installs.  Answers `[follower node events]`.\"\n   682\t  [follower node now]\n   683\t  (reduce (fn [[f n es] p]\n   684\t            (let [[f n polled] (poll f n p now)\n   685\t                  [f n settled] (settle f n p now)]\n   686\t              [f n (-> es (into polled) (into settled))]))\n   687\t          [follower node []]\n   688\t          (keys (:principals follower))))\n   689\t\n   690\t\n   691\t(defn install\n   692\t  \"Install `principal`'s confirmed head `trace` (5.7 step 3): it enters\n   693\t   the snapshot set, the floor moves to its sequence, its candidate\n   694\t   record is released, and `:installed` is emitted.  Any other trace is\n   695\t   refused `:yin.head/not-confirmed`, follower and node unchanged.\n   696\t   Answers `[follower node events]`.\"\n   697\t  [follower node principal trace]\n   698\t  (followed! follower principal)\n   699\t  (let [cand (get-in follower [:principals principal :candidate])]\n   700\t    (if-not (and cand (= :confirmed (:state cand)) (= trace (:trace cand)))\n   701\t      [follower node [(refused-event principal :yin.head/not-confirmed trace)]]\n   702\t      (let [[follower node] (release follower node principal (:manifest cand))]\n   703\t        [(update-in follower [:principals principal] assoc\n   704\t                    :installed trace :candidate nil)\n   705\t         (assoc-in node [ld/installed-key principal] (:manifest cand))\n   706\t         [{:yin.head/event :installed :principal principal :trace trace}]]))))\n   707\t\n   708\t\n   709\t;; =============================================================================\n   710\t;; Status, records and moved names (5.6, 5.7)\n   711\t;; =============================================================================\n   712\t\n   713\t(defn heads\n   714\t  \"Per followed principal: what is installed (`:installed` the trace,\n  1260\t  [node]\n  1261\t  (vec (sort-by str (filter #(loaded-datoms node %) (keys (:loads node))))))\n  1262\t\n  1263\t\n  1264\t(defn- walk-outcome\n  1265\t  \"The walk's answer, held to the three shapes: a throw is `walk-threw`,\n  1266\t   any other shape `walk-shape`.\"\n  1267\t  [walk handle]\n  1268\t  (let [v (try (walk handle)\n  1269\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n  1270\t                 {::walk :invalid :address nil\n  1271\t                  :defect {:code ::walk-threw :text (or (ex-message e) (str\n  1272\t                                                                         e))}}))\n  1273\t        defect (when (map? v) (:defect v))]\n  1274\t    (if (and (map? v)\n  1275\t             (case (::walk v)\n  1276\t               :missing (jing/segment-address? (:address v))\n  1277\t               :complete (contains? v :value)\n  1278\t               :invalid (and (map? defect) (keyword? (:code defect))\n  1279\t                             (or (nil? (:address v)) (jing/segment-address?\n  1280\t                                                       (:address v))))\n  1281\t               false))\n  1282\t      v\n  1283\t      {::walk :invalid :address nil :defect {:code ::walk-shape}})))\n  1284\t\n  1285\t\n  1286\t(defn- fail-load\n  1287\t  [node m reason]\n  1288\t  (let [{:keys [kind]} (get-in node [:loads m])]\n  1289\t    [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :failed :reason reason\n  1290\t                                              :fetching nil)\n  1291\t                                     (dissoc :walk)))\n  1292\t     [{::event :load-failed :manifest m :kind kind :reason reason}]]))\n  1293\t\n  1294\t\n  1295\t(defn- advance-load\n  1296\t  [node m done-by-id]\n  1297\t  (let [{:keys [fetching kind walk], :as record} (get-in node [:loads m])\n  1298\t        done (when fetching (get done-by-id (:id fetching)))]\n  1299\t    (cond\n  1300\t      (and fetching (nil? done)) [node []]\n  1301\t\n  1302\t      ;; the miss cause stays: another load may wait on the same address;\n  1303\t      ;; advance-loads drops it once none does\n  1304\t      (and done (not (:found? done)))\n  1305\t      (let [a (:address fetching)]\n  1306\t        (fail-load node m {::failure :miss :address a\n  1307\t                           :cause (get-in node [:misses a] ::dht/gap)}))\n  1308\t\n  1309\t      :else\n  1310\t      (let [fetched (cond-> (:fetched record) done inc)\n  1311\t            node (update-in node [:loads m] assoc :fetching nil :fetched\n  1312\t                            fetched)\n  1313\t            walked (walk-outcome walk (local node))]\n  1314\t        (case (::walk walked)\n  1315\t          :complete\n  1316\t          [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :loaded :value\n  1317\t                                                    (:value walked))\n  1318\t                                           (dissoc :walk)))\n  1319\t           [(cond-> {::event :loaded :manifest m :kind kind :fetched fetched}\n  1320\t              (= index-kind kind) (assoc :datoms (count (:value walked))))]]\n  1321\t\n  1322\t          :invalid\n  1323\t          (fail-load node m {::failure :invalid :address (:address walked)\n  1324\t                             :defect (:defect walked)})\n  1325\t\n  1326\t          :missing\n  1327\t          (let [a (:address walked)\n  1328\t                {:keys [outcome id], :as asked} (content.step/request-get\n  1329\t                                                  (:client node) a)]\n  1330\t            (case outcome\n  1331\t              (:requested :pending-request)\n  1332\t              [(-> node\n  1333\t                   (assoc :client (:state asked))\n  1334\t                   (assoc-in [:loads m :fetching] {:id id :address a}))\n  1335\t               []]\n  1336\t\n  1337\t              ;; the client still owes a request: ask again next step\n  1338\t              :busy [(assoc node :client (:state asked)) []]\n  1339\t\n  1340\t              (fail-load (assoc node :client (:state asked)) m\n  1341\t                         {::failure :unaskable :address a :outcome\n  1342\t                          outcome}))))))))\n  1343\t\n  1344\t\n  1345\t(defn- client-holds?\n  1346\t  \"Whether the load client holds an unsent request, an outstanding id or\n  1347\t   an undelivered completion: what an abandoned load leaves to drain.\"\n  1348\t  [client]\n  1349\t  (boolean (or (:unsent client)\n  1350\t               (seq (:outstanding client))\n  1351\t               (seq (:completed client)))))\n  1352\t\n  1353\t\n  1354\t(defn- advance-loads\n  1355\t  [node]\n  1356\t  (let [loading (sort-by str (keep (fn [[m r]]\n  1357\t                                     (when (= :loading (:status r))\n  1358\t                                       m))\n  1359\t                                   (:loads node)))]\n  1360\t    ;; the client is stepped while it holds anything, so what an abandon\n  1361\t    ;; leaves drains with no load active\n  1362\t    (if (or (and (empty? loading) (not (client-holds? (:client node))))\n  1363\t            (nil? (:dht node)))\n  1364\t      [node []]\n  1365\t      (let [{:keys [state completions]} (content.step/step (:client node)\n  1366\t                                                           fetch-budget)\n  1367\t            done-by-id (into {} (map (juxt :id identity)) completions)\n  1368\t            [node events] (reduce (fn [[node events] m]\n  1369\t                                    (let [[node more] (advance-load node m\n  1370\t                                                                    done-by-id)]\n  1371\t                                      [node (into events more)]))\n  1372\t                                  [(assoc node :client state) []]\n  1373\t                                  loading)]\n  1374\t        ;; every load waiting on an address has read its miss cause: keep\n  1375\t        ;; only the causes of addresses still being fetched\n  1376\t        [(update node :misses select-keys (fetching node)) events]))))\n  1377\t\n  1378\t\n  1379\t;; =============================================================================\n  1380\t;; The public step and reads\n  1381\t;; =============================================================================\n  1382\t\n  1383\t(defn step\n  1384\t  \"Advance the node once at the owner's millisecond reading `now`:\n  1385\t   append it as a tick; finish binding; admit repairs, then the puts and\n  1386\t   announcements on the ledger ring; release replicate requests; step\n  1387\t   the DHT; apply its facts; advance loads; and report publications.\n  1388\t   Answers `[node' events]`.  A refused node (its socket could not bind)\n  1389\t   is answered unchanged.\"\n  1390\t  [node now]\n  1391\t  (if (:refusal node)\n  1392\t    [node []]\n  1393\t    (let [node (tick node now)\n  1394\t          [node bound] (bind-step node)\n  1395\t          node (admit-repairs node)\n  1396\t          [node unknown] (admit-ledger node)\n  1397\t          node (release node)\n  1398\t          node (cond-> node (:dht node) (update :dht dht/step step-budget))\n  1399\t          [node lost] (read-facts node)\n  1400\t          [node loaded] (advance-loads node)\n  1401\t          [node reported] (settle-publications node)]\n  1402\t      [node (-> bound (into unknown) (into lost) (into loaded) (into\n  1403\t                                                                 reported))])))\n  1404\t\n  1405\t\n  1406\t(defn refusal\n  1407\t  \"Why the node stopped (its socket could not bind), or nil.\"\n  1408\t  [node]\n  1409\t  (:refusal node))\n  1410\t\n  1411\t\n  1412\t(defn backlog\n  1413\t  \"What the node retains now: queue entries (`:fresh`, `:repair`),\n  1414\t   requests outstanding (`:outstanding`, split `:outstanding-fresh` and\n  1415\t   `:outstanding-repair`), live publications (`:live`), those awaiting a\n  1416\t   first report (`:open`) and repairing (`:repairing`), and the ledger\n  1417\t   entries they hold (`:ledger-entries`).\"\n  1418\t  [node]\n  1419\t  {:fresh (count (:fresh node))\n  1420\t   :repair (count (:repair node))\n  1421\t   :outstanding (count (:inflight node))\n  1422\t   :outstanding-fresh (in-flight node :fresh)\n  1423\t   :outstanding-repair (in-flight node :repair)\n  1424\t   :live (count (:pubs node))\n  1425\t   :open (open-count node)\n  1426\t   :repairing (count (filter repairing? (:pubs node)))\n  1427\t   :ledger-entries (reduce + 0 (map :blobs (:pubs node)))})\n  1428\t\n  1429\t\n  1430\t(defn- summary\n  1431\t  [node pub]\n  1432\t  {:manifest (:manifest pub)\n  1433\t   :blobs (:blobs pub)\n  1434\t   :sent (:sent pub)\n  1435\t   :result (result pub)\n  1436\t   :reported? (:reported? pub)\n  1437\t   :repairing? (repairing? pub)\n  1438\t   :delay (:delay pub)\n  1439\t   :due (:due pub)\n  1440\t   :cycles (:cycles pub)\n  1441\t   :cycle-open? (some? (:cycle pub))\n  1442\t   :repair-queued (held-in-repair node (:id pub))\n  1443\t   :entries (:entries pub)})\n  1444\t\n  1445\t\n  1446\t(defn publications\n  1447\t  \"Every live publication, oldest first, as data: its result, counts,\n  1448\t   repair state and ledger entries.\"\n  1449\t  [node]\n  1450\t  (mapv #(summary node %) (:pubs node)))\n  1451\t\n  1452\t\n  1453\t(defn publication\n  1454\t  \"The oldest live publication of `manifest-address`, as `publications`\n  1455\t   answers it, or nil.\"\n  1456\t  [node manifest-address]\n  1457\t  (some #(when (= manifest-address (:manifest %)) (summary node %)) (:pubs\n  1458\t                                                                      node)))\n  1459\t\n  1460\t\n  1461\t(defn busy?\n  1462\t  \"True while the node owes its owner an event or holds work: binding, a\n  1463\t   load, unread puts, a first report owed, or an address queued or\n  1464\t   outstanding.  A publication waiting for its next repair cycle does\n  1465\t   not make the node busy.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
