{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-05 16:34:48 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-05 23:34:48 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a10ce5-0fa6-7e62-b94d-9f7d5c9ab3e1\n\nP1 | [head.cljc:636](src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:636) | A signed, verified trace can crash the follower during confirmation. Reproduced using a hash-valid manifest whose four roots contain `[[100 :x/y 1 0 0] [101 :x/y 1 \"bad-t\" 0]]`. The [covered-index walk](src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:1130) checks counts without validating rows and reports `:complete`; `head/step` then throws `ClassCastException` through `seq-of`. Restoring the same trace through `follow` also throws without a startup refusal naming the principal ([line 307](src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:307)). | Validate persisted datom rows inside the covered-index walk, returning `:index-invalid` for malformed rows. Add follower and restart regressions asserting failure as data, unchanged floor, and no installation.\n\nP2 | [dht_test.cljc:850](test/dao/space/dht_test.cljc:850) | The late-answer test does not prove that the injected answer is dropped. Retirement leaves no load or client interest; [advance-loads:1362](src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:1362) therefore skips the client on every subsequent step. The answer remains unread while the no-blob/no-event assertions pass. | Force client polling after injecting the retired answer and assert unsolicited-answer handling. Also reload the same address, withhold its new answer, inject the old answer, and assert that the new load cannot complete from it.\n\nThe ownership/release paths, confirmation/install separation, snapshot exclusion, refusal translation, and unchanged `forget` otherwise match the reviewed contract. Targeted malformed stream values—including odd lists and malformed envelope/proof maps—were refused without throwing. The wrong-sequence arrival orders, unfinished load, and durable-before-used tests assert meaningful resulting states.\n\nThe engineer’s four unresolved concerns are accurate; I leave the three designated questions to the Architect. The fourth correctly distinguishes client retirement from the DHT’s independent [blob storage](src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc:837). Section 4.3’s amendment is necessary to replace its obsolete cross-kind no-op rule. Tracked changes match the named files; additional untracked files are collaboration logs/prompts.\n\n`deposit!`’s last-signed protection depends on retaining the board: an empty replacement ring loses that evidence ([head.cljc:218](src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:218)). No replacement path is implemented in H1. Node and Dart remain unverified; they should exercise numeric behavior, reader conditionals, exception handling, and portable reader tests. EDN rendering belongs to H3.\n\nBlockers: fix malformed-index crashes and strengthen late-answer verification; then pass Node and Dart and land the Architect rulings."}}
